    "https://davenport.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/15/home/requisition/3238?c=davenport": {
      "title": "(Student) Unpaid Internship Workstudy Only - copy",
      "description": "(Student) Unpaid Internship Workstudy Only - copy | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) (Student) Unpaid Internship Workstudy Only - copy Grand Rapids, MI, United States | req3238 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/16/2026 Back to Search Work Study Eligible Students Completing Unpaid Internships or Volunteering CLASSIFICATION: Student Employee STATUS: Temporary, Non-exempt PAYRANGE: $20.00 DEPARTMENT: Various LOCATION: Various Not for Profit Offsite Locations REPORTS TO: Associate Director, Employee Experience Attention Work Study Eligible Students : Federal Work-Study provides part-time jobs for undergraduate and graduate students with financial need, allowing them to earn money to help pay education expenses. The program encourages community service work and work related to the student’s course of study. JOB SUMMARY: Job duties vary based on position. Please indicate your areas of interest in your application (IT, Marketing, Paralegal, Human Resources, Finance, Reading Tutor, Other). This position is for students who qualify for work study funding and are completing unpaid internships at qualifying non-profit organizations or who are currently volunteering at a qualified non-profit organization that are giving direct service to the community the non-profit serves. QUALIFICATIONS: Must be enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours as an undergraduate student or 3 credit hours as a graduate student while meeting the standards of academic progress. Students must be work study eligible based on their current year's FAFSA. Pay will stop when work study funds are exausted. Sites must be non-profit sites that provide direct service to the community. SEIND19 Apply Now Share Save Job"
