      "title": "Student) Team Assistant Baseball",
      "description": "Student) Team Assistant Baseball | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Student) Team Assistant Baseball Grand Rapids, MI, United States | req3236 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/10/2026 Back to Search At Davenport University, we know what it takes to be successful. With over 150 years of providing quality education under our belts, thousands of Davenport graduates are making an impact on the world with the knowledge and skills they learned here. Our team of faculty and staff collaborate to make this possible. Joining DU means growing and advancing your own career, while making a lasting impact on our students, colleagues and the communities in which we serve. Would you like to be part of our success? It all starts here! Student) Team Assistant Baseball WORK LOCATION: Grand Rapids - Lettinga Campus DEPARTMENT: Athletics-Administration POSITION PAY RANGE: $13.73 TARGET HIRING RANGE: Actual pay offered will be commensurate with candidate qualifications and experience, the type of role, pay equity and available funding. SUMMARY: This position acts as a general assistant to the department, performing clerical office functions related to daily operations and will be responsible for duties related to game management. The Athletic Assistant will serve as the student team manager and will work closely with the assigned team providing an array of team related services. The position requires the employee to be self-motivated, be familiar with and competent within the athletic department and be responsible to work with minimum supervision.  These responsibilities are performed in an ethical manner consistent with the University’s mission, vision, and values which include diversity, equity and inclusion. RESPONSIBILITIES: Film games, video recording, editing, and provide highlights for the team. Track and monitor team equipment distribution to players, will be responsible for all equipment and inventory. Set-up and breakdown for games. Generate team statistics reports for coaches. Coordinate travel including hotel, restaurant, game and practice sites. Responsible for team laundry. Responsible for creating, maintaining and updating files and record keeping systems. Generate reports, memorandums, correspondence, presentation materials, spreadsheets and graphics, and other materials using various software programs. Sort and distribute incoming mail and faxes. Copy and collate documents. Assemble informational packets. Assists with special events and functions as needed. May be responsible for greeting visitors, as well as answering and routing incoming calls. Scheduling and confirming appointments. Handling of documents and maintaining a high level of confidentiality. Conducts special projects, research and assignments as assigned. Provides GREAT customer service, anticipating and exceeding the needs of our customers. Demonstrate and promote the University Cultural Values. Understand and abide by all external and internal regulations and policies.  This includes NCAA, GLIAC and national affiliations associated within athletics or other role specific regulations. Perform other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS: High School Diploma or GED equivalent. Must be enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours and meeting the standards of academic progress. Experience in office setting preferred but not required. Demonstrated ability to work accurately and effectively with computerized data systems (PC and mainframe). Demonstrated ability to work effectively with people of diverse backgrounds and promote a positive working environment, spirit of cooperation and positive reactions to change and conflict resolution. Demonstrated excellent interpersonal, communication and presentation skills, both written and oral which transcend diverse audiences. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and relate well to students, parents, faculty, staff, and others while maintaining appropriate confidentiality. Demonstrated motivational and problem solving capabilities with a high degree of integrity, ethics, and dedication to the mission of the University. Business office environment. Prolonged sitting and standing. Use of personal computer and telephone (eye and hand strain). Some travel between locations may be required (own transportation). No regular lifting requirements, occasional lifting up to 50 pounds. SEIND19 Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://davenport.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/15/home/requisition/3235?c=davenport": {
      "title": "ADA Testing Oversight",
      "description": "ADA Testing Oversight | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) ADA Testing Oversight Lansing, MI, United States | req3235 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/10/2026 Back to Search ADA Testing Oversight STATUS: Limited Part-time DEPARTMENT : Admin-Student Affairs LOCATION: Lansing Michigan Campus REPORTS TO : Campus Director Pay: $15.60/hour SUMMARY: This position partners with the Student Access Department at Davenport University to oversee ADA related testing accommodations. The Testing Coordinator will work with the accommodation approved students and their faculty to schedule testing in the designated location at their specific campus. In addition, the Testing Coordinator will set up the appropriate ADA accommodations, coordinate the testing check in/check out process, and proctor the assessments. The Testing Coordinator will need to be detail oriented as they manage the documentation related to both designated testing location data and accommodations, and be able to execute procedures communicated to them . These responsibilities are performed in an ethical manner consistent with the University’s mission, vision, and values which include diversity, equity and inclusion. RESPONSIBILITIES: Train, certify, and keep updated certifications for testing network partnerships that Davenport University maintains to deliver educational exams. Understand and abide by the designated testing location guidelines, and the procedures for each exam scheduled in conjunction with the faculty requests . Maintain the confidentiality and security of the tests and the testing environment, as well as student disability related accommodations. Provide proctoring to all testing that occurs within the designated testing space. R eport any occurrences that fall outside designated testing area guidelines to the Office of Student Conduct . Maintain the confidentiality o f all testing candidates and th eir subject matter . Greet students , verify identification, explain the testing process, assist with third party software management to begin/end a test, and help examinees with technical issues during testing. Provide all appropriate accommodations for each student as outlined by their approved disability documentation . Enter data and maintain attendance records through various computer software programs such as Microsoft Office and Google Suites technology. Communicate with D avenport University partners in a professional and timely manner including but not limited to faculty and the Student Access staff. Demonstrate a calm, professional, positive and friendly demeanor throughout the testing process answering questions tactfully and appropriately. Understand and abide by all external and internal regulations and policies.  This includes NCAA, GLIAC and national affiliations associated within athletics or other role specific regulations. Provide GREAT customer service, anticipating and exceeding the needs of our customers. Demonstrate and promote the University ’s Cultural Values. Perform other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS: High School Diploma required, Bachelor’s Degree preferred. Prior proctoring experience preferred. Demonstrated ability to learn , follow and ex ecute established procedures and guidelines. Demonstrated ability to set and accomplish goals, work under pressure and meet deadlines; attention to detail and multi-tasking skills a must. Demonstrated ability to operate a variety of office equipment (printer, copier, fax, scanner). Demonstrated strong customer service commitment with specific experience with students preferred. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with people of diverse backgrounds and promote a positive working environment, spirit of cooperation and positive reactions to change and conflict resolution . Excellent interpersonal, communication and presentation skills, both written and oral which transcend diverse audiences. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and relate well to donors, alumni, students, parents, faculty, staff, and others while maintaining appropriate confidentiality. Demonstrated motivational and problem - solving capabilities with a high degree of integrity, ethics, and dedication to the mission of the University. Strong work ethic. Ability to pass a pre-employment background investigation including but not limited to: standard criminal background check and employment reference checks. Select positions may be subject to drug/alcohol screening. Business office environment. Prolonged sitting and standing. Use of personal computer and telephone (eye and hand strain) . Some travel between campuses required (own transportation) No regular lifting requirements , occasional lifting up to 25 pounds. Must be able to work an irregular schedule, evenings or Saturday as needed, additional hours during peak times or as required. Davenport University is committed to building and supporting a diverse community of students, faculty and staff.  Davenport University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees, applicants and students without unlawful discrimination based on national origin, race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability, gender identity, veteran, or military status, marital status, height, weight, genetic information, or other protected status DAVENPORT UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER Revision Date: 9/ 25 / 20 23 Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://davenport.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/15/home/requisition/3227?c=davenport": {
      "title": "(Student) K-8 Tutor-Refugee Center",
      "description": "(Student) K-8 Tutor-Refugee Center | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) (Student) K-8 Tutor-Refugee Center Grand Rapids, MI, United States | req3227 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/25/2026 Back to Search Project Faulu After-school Program Facilitator (Tutor) CLASSIFICATION: Student Employee PAYRANGE: $20.00 DEPARTMENT: Community Work Study/ Career Services LOCATION: 860 Woodfield E Dr. SE Grand Rapids, MI 49508) REPORTS TO : Manager - Employee Experience & Benefits REC Mission Statement: We support refugees in their journey to become fully participating members of the West Michigan community. We envision a thriving, multicultural West Michigan community where all have an opportunity to pursue a better future! Summary: The Refugee Education Center (REC) after-school program is called Project Faulu, which means success in Swahili. Project Faulu volunteers work closely with the K-12 Programs staff and a team of other volunteers to provide a supportive and engaging learning environment for students with a refugee background. Project Faulu is our K-8 program designed specifically for children with a refugee background, focusing on language and culture, creativity and inquiry, academic engagement, and positive social skills. Our goal is to provide students with opportunities to learn in a community of peers and volunteers. Project Faulu Facilitators are responsible for welcoming students in the afterschool program, facilitating games, snack time & discussions, thematic activities designed by program staff, and reading to and with students. The Project Faulu Program runs on Monday-Wednesday from 3:45pm-6:30pm. Volunteers must volunteer at least one day per week, preferably two. Training: Initial and ongoing training/check-ins are required. Training will be held on Tuesday, September 1 from 5:30-8:30pm and Wednesday, September 2 from 1:30-4:30pm (choose one to attend). ALL volunteers, including returning volunteers and interns, must attend one training session. Volunteer Duties: Commit to volunteering consistently on a weekly basis, for the duration of at least one full semester Review activity plans of session to ensure comprehension of activities and materials in advance Facilitate activities with up to three students per session Support and engage K-8 students attending the Refugee Education Center by: Engaging fully in all elements of the daily schedule, such as games, snack & discussion, thematic activities, reading time, clean up and reporting Facilitating thematic activities designed by program staff Reading diverse, multicultural books with students Engaging students in additional activities such as puzzles, homework support, projects, creative assignments, or any other appropriate activities to support their learning needs Willingness and interest in learning about student home languages and cultures Complete daily reporting immediately after conclusion of each volunteering session Demonstrate teamwork and integrity with staff, fellow volunteers, students, and their families Ensure a safe and clean learning environment through assisting with program set up and after-program clean up. Attend all required training courses. Report issues of concern to K-12 Programs staff Understand and abide by all external and internal regulations and policies.  This includes NCAA, GLIAC and national affiliations associated within athletics or other role specific regulations. Provide GREAT customer service, anticipating and exceeding the needs of our customers. Demonstrate and promote the University’s Cultural Values. Perform other duties as assigned. Desired Qualifications: Must be work study eligible Must be enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours as an undergraduate student or 3 credit hours as a graduate student while meeting the standards of academic progress Must be a Michigan Resident or have temporary residency in Michigan Willingness and ability to pass State and Federal background checks Some leadership or support experience Demonstrated motivational and problem solving capabilities with a high degree of integrity, ethics, and dedication to the mission of the University Classroom and Office environment.  Prolonged sitting and standing.  Use of personal computer and telephone (eye and hand strain). Some travel between locations may be required (own transportation).  No regular lifting requirements, occasional lifting up to 15 pounds. Preferred Skills & Competencies: Ability to work with diverse populations and make students feel welcomed and safe Self-motivation to identify and support students in their educational and social emotional needs Documenting the activities of their assigned level through picture taking and sharing pictures with the K-12 Programs staff Ability to communicate to K-12 Programs staff on successes and challenges faced (including what went well and didn’t go well with the various activities) DAVENPORT UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER SEIND19 Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://davenport.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/15/home/requisition/3226?c=davenport": {
      "title": "Peer Mentor 2026",
      "description": "Peer Mentor 2026 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Peer Mentor 2026 Grand Rapids, MI, United States | req3226 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/24/2026 Back to Search TITLE OF POSITION : Peer Mentor DEPARTMENT: Academics LOCATION: W.A. Lettinga Campus REPORTS TO: Director of Student Transitions and Academic Readiness SUMMARY: The Peer-Mentoring Program partners sophomore, junior and senior students, with first-year first generation students. It is proven that if first-year students have meaningful interactions with a positive mentor, their motivation and academic performance are significantly increased. A mentor will listen and encourage their mentee to utilize resources available to achieve academic success. A mentor functions as a coach, friend and most importantly a positive role model. The program supports and encourages students in meeting their personal and educational goals. RESPONSIBILITIES: Meet bi-weekly with mentee Abide by DU employee handbook Attend peer mentor training and monthly meetings Offer relevant experience and learning skills Provide a positive and affirming environment Model flexibility and a positive growth mindset Dedicate adequate and consistent time with mentee Keep records of meetings and share with the director Respect confidentiality Report any concerns to the Dir of Student Transitions and Academic Readiness (STAR) or, if applicable Student Care report to Student Life Meet with Dir of STAR and seek feedback on effectiveness of their mentoring role Provides GREAT customer service, anticipating and exceeding the needs of our customers. Understand and abide by all external and internal regulations and policies.  This includes NCAA, GLIAC and national affiliations associated within athletics or other role specific regulations. Demonstrate and promote the University Cultural Values. Perform other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS: Must be enrolled in a minimum of 6 credits as an undergraduate student or 3 credits as a graduate student. Must be meeting Standards of Academic Progress (SAP). Excellent interpersonal skills that transcend diverse audiences; communicating to university customers with positive attitudes toward change, confidentiality, and conflict resolution. Must be highly motivated and solution oriented with a high degree of integrity, ethics, and dedication to the mission of the University. Must be able to work an irregular schedule, evenings or Saturday as needed, additional hours during peak times or as required. Business office environment. Prolonged sitting and standing. Use of personal computer and telephone (eye and hand strain). DAVENPORT UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER Revised: 11/9/2018 SEIND19 Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://davenport.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/15/home/requisition/3220?c=davenport": {
      "title": "Career & Internship Coach",
      "description": "Career & Internship Coach | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Career & Internship Coach Grand Rapids, MI, United States | req3220 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/18/2026 Back to Search Career & Internship Coach The Office of Career & Personal Development. STATUS: Full-time, Exempt LOCATION: Grand Rapids Lettinga Campus REPORTS TO : The Office of Career & Personal Development. SALARY: Up to $53,000 ***Actual salary will be commensurate with experience. SUMMARY: This position provides excellent service to students and alumni for their career preparation and advancement needs.  Their primary objectives are to help students with all aspects of professional development as well as assisting students in finding employment both during their education and after graduation and support students’ long-term career goals. Career Coaches develop and maintain strategic employer partnerships to create a robust pipeline of industry opportunities (e.g., jobs, internships) for students and recent graduates. These responsibilities are performed in an ethical manner consistent with the University’s mission, vision, and values that include diversity, equity and inclusion. RESPONSIBILITIES: The required activities and tasks of this role will be successfully completed by effectively utilizing key career services technology platforms (i.e. PathwayU Assessments, Handshake, and Quinncia AI) and the Google Workspace for support and execution. Coach students and alumni through the career development process, including identifying professional goals, mastering critical job search skills, and implementing effective employment strategies . Provide one-on-one coaching to students and alumni to facilitate the identification, securing, and, when applicable, approval management of experiential learning opportunities (e.g., internships, practicum) in support of on-time graduation and long-term career success. Collaborate with faculty and advisors to ensure the appropriate experience is gained between internships / practicums, 489 project course work or Credit for Prior Learning. Assist students and alumni in the development, review, and modification of résumés and other application documents to ensure it is in accordance with industry, ethical, and currently accepted human resources guidelines including professional writing assistance, for resumes, CV’s Cover Letters, letters of inquiry, writing samples and thank you letters. Conduct mock interviews and share interview insights with students and alumni. Assist them with current interview techniques, practice software and conducting informal interviews and providing practice and career interviews with employers on and off campus and providing constructive feedback. Provide career-related job search techniques and assist with job search strategies, teach job-matching skills and offer job referral services to empower students and alumni with the essential skills and resources required for successful post-graduation employment and long-term career attainment. Provide assistance to students and alumni in securing full and part-time career related employment and experiential opportunities through individual appointment, classroom presentations, workshops seminars and best-in-class job search sites. Collaborate with faculty by offering effective classroom presentations, event collaboration and data on hiring employers. Support the execution of career events by handling specific assigned tasks such as preparing promotional materials, managing RSVP lists, and helping with on-site setup and teardown. Understand and abide by all external and internal regulations and policies associated within Career Services and Career Coaching standards or other role specific regulations including NACE and CDF standards of ethics for career development, coaching and facilitation. Support university Vision, Mission and values through providing end-to-end support for other student services teams including admissions, athletics, and residence life. Demonstrate a willingness to grow, change, and shift daily work as roles adjust to industry, student and university needs. Understand and abide by all external and internal regulations and policies.  This includes NCAA, GLIAC and national affiliations associated within athletics or other role specific knowledge. Provides GREAT customer service, anticipating and exceeding the needs of our customers. Demonstrate and promote the University Cultural Values. Perform other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree required. Career Development, Career Coach or Employment Specialist credentials preferred or acquired within 2 years of hire. 1-3 years of experience in a student-facing role within higher education, such as admissions, student activities, academic advising, student services, or working in industry as a career counselor, coach, or recruiter. Experience delivering workshops or presentations to groups on topics related to professional development, communication skills, or college readiness. Practical experience in providing direct guidance (e.g., mentoring, tutoring, peer advising) to individuals on decision-making or skill development. Familiarity with or exposure to career services functions, including resume/cover letter review, job search strategies, or career fair coordination. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with people of diverse backgrounds and work styles, and promote a positive working environment, spirit of cooperation and positive reactions to change and conflict resolution. Demonstrated ability to effectively plan, meet deadlines and accomplish goals. Excellent interpersonal, communication and presentation skills, both written and oral which transcend diverse audiences. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and relate well to employers , alumni, students, parents, faculty, staff and others while maintaining professionalism and appropriate confidentiality. Demonstrated problem solving capabilities with a high degree of integrity, ethics, and dedication to the mission of the university. Business office environment.  Prolonged sitting and standing.  Use of personal computer and telephone (eye and hand strain).  Some travel between locations required (own transportation). No regular lifting requirements, occasional lifting up to 25 pounds. Strong work ethic. Demonstrated ability to work accurately and effectively with computerized data systems. Must be able to work an irregular schedule, evenings or Saturday as needed, additional hours during peak times or as required. Davenport University is committed to building and supporting a diverse community of students, faculty and staff.  Davenport University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees, applicants and students without unlawful discrimination based on national origin, race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability, gender identity, veteran, or military status, marital status, height, weight, genetic information, or other protected status DAVENPORT UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER Revision Date:  1/05/2026 Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://davenport.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/15/home/requisition/3217?c=davenport": {
      "title": "Limited Part Time Public Safety Officer - Midland",
      "description": "Limited Part Time Public Safety Officer - Midland | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Limited Part Time Public Safety Officer - Midland Midland, MI, United States | req3217 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/13/2026 Back to Search Limited Part Time Public Safety Officer STATUS: Limited Part-time, Hours ranging from 0 - 28/week DEPARTMENT: Public Safety LOCATION: Great Lakes Bay Campus, Midland Michigan REPORTS TO: Public Safety Supervisor Pay: $19.00 - $20.00/hr Summary This position is charged with providing a safe and secure environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. \n        This position works to educate the campus community regarding safety and security, minimize risk for the University, and enforce all University policies and procedures. \n        These responsibilities are performed in an ethical manner consistent with the University’s mission, vision, and values which include diversity, equity, and inclusion. Responsibilities Provide proactive campus patrols following the department’s community policing model. Enforce university rules and regulations on campus, which include conducting investigations and completing/filing necessary documentation. Take immediate action to protect the life safety of community members, including other Public Safety Department personnel. Deliver medical treatment including basic first aid, CPR, and use of an AED unit, following training and certification. Perform safety escorts for students and employees to their cars and/or from building to building. Provide security for dignitaries and other visitors to the University. Investigate and file reports of security and safety concerns involving building structures, yards, and parking lots on campus. Identify and take steps to address safety hazards and liability concerns. Complete thorough incident reports on violations of laws or university policy, safety hazards or liability concerns, medical emergencies, and employee injuries. Maintain physical security systems including but not limited to: Electronic Access Control, CCTV, and Keys. Regulate and monitor traffic and parking conditions, taking enforcement action in concert with university policy. Maintain an inventory of found property following department policy. Understand and abide by all external and internal regulations and policies. Provides GREAT customer service, anticipating and exceeding the needs of our customers. Demonstrates and promotes the University’s Cultural Values. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications High School Diploma (or equivalent) required, Associates degree preferred. No conviction for any felony offense, or misdemeanor crime of domestic violence. No conviction within the previous 3 years for possession/use of illegal drugs, criminal alcohol offenses, or any criminal driving offense. A valid driver’s license is required in the state assigned (Michigan). Must maintain an acceptable driving record as required by the university insurer. Must have, or be eligible to obtain, a Michigan Concealed Pistol License. Must be able to maintain certification in First Aid/CPR/AED, defensive tactics – including the use of OC Spray and handcuffs. Must maintain a level of physical fitness suitable for the effective performance of all job-related functions. Ability to pass a pre-employment background investigation including criminal background check and drug/alcohol screening. 20/20 vision – with or without correction, normal peripheral vision, depth perception, and ability to distinguish colors. Ability to professionally respond to incidents and effectively present findings through formal reports. Strong report-writing skills. Proficiency with computers, email systems, Google Drive, and other department technology resources. Foundational knowledge of legal and compliance requirements, especially: Title IX, The Cleary Act, and FERPA. Service-oriented with an exceptional customer service attitude at all times. Ability to work independently, without direct supervision. Ability to work in extreme temperatures and weather conditions. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with people of diverse backgrounds. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and presentation skills, both written and oral. Strong work ethic and high degree of integrity. Physical requirements include prolonged sitting/standing, climbing stairs/ladders, and lifting up to 25 lbs. daily. Must be able to work an irregular schedule, including evenings, weekends, and holidays. DAVENPORT UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER Davenport University is committed to building and supporting a diverse community of students, faculty and staff.  Davenport University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees, applicants and students without unlawful discrimination based on national origin, race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability, gender identity, veteran, or military status, marital status, height, weight, genetic information, or other protected status Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://davenport.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/15/home/requisition/3216?c=davenport": {
      "title": "(Student) Campus Life Assistant",
      "description": "(Student) Campus Life Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) (Student) Campus Life Assistant Grand Rapids, MI, United States | req3216 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/11/2026 Back to Search At Davenport University, we know what it takes to be successful. With over 150 years of providing quality education under our belts, thousands of Davenport graduates are making an impact on the world with the knowledge and skills they learned here. Our team of faculty and staff collaborate to make this possible. Joining DU means growing and advancing your own career, while making a lasting impact on our students, colleagues and the communities in which we serve. Would you like to be part of our success? It all starts here! (Student) Campus Life Assistant WORK LOCATION: Grand Rapids - Lettinga Campus DEPARTMENT: CCL-Student Life POSITION PAY RANGE: $13.73 TARGET HIRING RANGE: Actual pay offered will be commensurate with candidate qualifications and experience, the type of role, pay equity and available funding. SUMMARY: As a part of the Center for Campus Life (CCL), a Campus Life Assistant will assist in the oversight of our front desk and serve as the point person for those entering the CCL. The individual would answer and direct phone calls appropriately on behalf of all members of the CCL team, and/or assisting any student, staff, or faculty member that comes to the office for support. The student would serve as a source of general information to other students on topics and questions related to all departments within the Center for Campus Life. Specifically, the Student Life Assistant will support the Student Life team to identify the needs and interests of the student population in order to provide a wide range of quality engagement opportunities. The Student Life Assistant will be a resource for students interested in Registered Student Organizations and programming. RESPONSIBILITIES: Perform routine office duties including front desk phone service, file management, appointment scheduling, and project completion for Center for Campus Life staff members. Make connections with community partners to establish community service opportunities for Davenport students. Handle phone calls, conversations, and database documents on behalf of Campus Life utilizing the highest level of confidentiality at all times. > Design flyers and promotional materials for events, programs, and the office in general. Maintain and develop a social media presence for Student Life and Campus Life with content creation and online engagement. Assist with maintaining content of Engage@DU, the student engagement platform. Set up and work informational tables for events in academic buildings and/or Dining Hall. Maintain up to date posters and other promotional materials in approved areas around campus. Assist in the development and organization of social opportunities for students to connect with one another and the Davenport community. Serve as a resource for students by connecting them with leadership opportunities including Registered Student Organizations (RSOs), Campus Activities Board (CAB), and Student Government. Assist with on-site management of campus events while tracking attendance and providing program evaluation. Provide support for the Panther Resource Closet (PRC) by assisting with inventory maintenance and tracking. Understand and abide by all external and internal regulations and policies. Develop and maintain skills by participating in ongoing training seminars. QUALIFICATIONS: Must maintain a GPA of 2.5 or higher. Must be enrolled at least half time (6 credits undergrad and 3 credits grad) at Davenport University. Must be meeting Standards of Academic Progress (SAP). Must be work study eligible. Must demonstrate the ability to perform well in the area of customer service, especially in a high traffic and busy environment. Demonstrated ability to effectively plan, develop goals, meet deadlines, and accomplish goals while prioritizing workloads. Demonstrated ability to maintain a professional appearance and manner. Must be able to work an irregular schedule, evenings or Saturday as needed, additional hours during peak times or as required. Excellent interpersonal skills that transcend diverse audiences; communicating to university customers with positive attitudes toward change, confidentiality, and conflict resolution. Must be highly motivated and solution-oriented with a high degree of integrity, ethics, and dedication to the mission of the university. Business office environment. Prolonged sitting and standing. Use of personal computer and telephone (eye and hand strain). Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
